{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"carried_from":"prior-1","checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a block_impact() case with a would-block finding at validity < 0.5 asserting val_lt_half == 1 (and one that also has a None-validity would-block finding to pin the skip).","criteria":["tests"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["docs/experiments/calibrate_code_review_thresholds.py:132-137: `v = f.get(\"validity\"); if v is None: continue; validities.append(float(v)); if float(v) < 0.5: low_validity += 1`","tests/unit/test_code_review_criteria_routing.py:243: `assert result[\"val_lt_half\"] == 0`","Synthetic corpus (lines 210-231) contains no would-block finding with validity < 0.5, and the empty-corpus test (line 246) yields 0 by vacuity, so the increment branch is never taken under test.","criteria_routing.json _comment cites 'none below 0.5' as a flip justification, and code-review-threshold-calibration.md records 'val<0.5 | 0' as decision-relevant — the column is contract-bearing but its non-zero path is unverified."],"finding":"The block_impact() `val_lt_half` counter (would-block findings with validity < 0.5) is never exercised by a non-zero case: both synthetic-corpus tests assert `val_lt_half == 0`. This column is the load-bearing 'none below 0.5' justification cited in the routing JSON _comment and the calibration document, so a regression in the low-validity counting (wrong operator, off-by-one, or the `if v is None: continue` skipping the count) would ship undetected.","id":"1","impact":0.27,"location":"tests/unit/test_code_review_criteria_routing.py:243","norm_id":"n115b105d8fa2a7e7","priority":0.2314,"reason":"default-advisory","reviewer_id":"code-review-tests","reviewers":["code-review-tests"],"scenarios":["A refactor flips the comparison to `> 0.5` or `<= 0.5`, or the None-skip accidentally bypasses the low-validity count; every existing test still passes because val_lt_half stays 0.","The calibration table would then report an incorrect val<0.5 count, silently mis-justifying a blocking flip."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a synthetic-corpus variant with a surviving finding at priority>=0.54 and validity 0.3, asserting `result['val_lt_half'] == 1` and that it is excluded from `mean_validity`; optionally add a None-validity would-block finding to confirm it is skipped from both `validities` and `low_validity`.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"local","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":false,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"medium","escapes_automation":true,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":false,"implicit_coupling":false,"likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":true,"removed_public_symbol":false,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":true,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_decision":false,"trigger_likelihood":"rare","unversioned_published_contract_break":false,"version_signal_present":false}}}],"blocking":[],"change_fingerprint":"6f090a4940b1d62c","change_id":"Ie2b2bb52e7097dd1f83fff48ea0fc